To set up monitoring for BGP neighbor connections and metrics on your Nokia 7750 SR, start by entering the BMP (BGP Monitoring Protocol) configuration context. Use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure
bmp
```

This places you in the BMP configuration mode, where you can define monitoring stations, specify parameters like `route-monitoring`, and activate the protocol. For example, to add a monitoring station:

```cli
station "Station1"
  connection
    local-address 192.0.2.1
    remote-address 203.0.113.5 12345
  exit
  route-monitoring post-policy
  no shutdown
exit
```

You can then apply BMP to specific BGP neighbors or groups under their respective configuration contexts using the `monitor` command. For instance:

```cli
router bgp
  group "BGP_Group"
    monitor "Station1"
    exit
  exit
```
