To make your BGP sessions tolerate brief link flapping without immediately tearing down, use these commands:

```
configure router bgp
    disable-fast-external-failover
    damp-peer-oscillations
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `disable-fast-external-failover` stops BGP from instantly dropping sessions when a physical link fails. Instead, BGP waits for the hold timer (default 90 seconds) to expire, allowing short blips to recover.  
- `damp-peer-oscillations` adds progressive delays between session reestablishment attempts after repeated failures, using default timers:  
  - First failure: 0-minute delay (immediate retry)  
  - Subsequent failures: 5-minute delay (doubling each time, max 60 minutes)  
  - Resets after 30 error-free minutes.  

Apply these at the global BGP level to affect all peers, or target specific groups/neighbors if needed. No hold-time adjustments are required.
