To set the BGP hold time to a maximum of 2 minutes while allowing negotiation down to 1 minute, configure the hold-time with the `min` parameter at the appropriate BGP level (global, group, or neighbor):

```console
configure router bgp
    hold-time 120 min 60
```

**Explanation:**  
- `hold-time 120` sets the **proposed hold-time** to 120 seconds (2 minutes).  
- `min 60` sets the **minimum acceptable hold-time** to 60 seconds (1 minute). Peers proposing values below 60 seconds will be rejected.  

This ensures sessions negotiate between 60-120 seconds without compatibility issues. Apply this command under:
- `config>router>bgp` (global)  
- `config>router>bgp>group` (group-specific)  
- `config>router>bgp>group>neighbor` (neighbor-specific)  

**Example for a specific neighbor:**  
```console
configure router bgp 
    neighbor 192.0.2.1 
        hold-time 120 min 60
```
