To automatically tag outgoing BGP routes with a metric of 15000 only when the original route lacks a metric, configure a policy that sets the MED (Multi-Exit Discriminator) under `policy-options` and apply it as an export policy to BGP neighbors:

```cli
/configure router policy-options
begin
policy-statement set-default-med
    entry 10
        condition not med
        action accept
            set med 15000
        exit
    exit
    entry 20
        action accept
        exit
    exit
commit
```

Apply the policy to BGP groups or neighbors:
```cli
/configure router bgp
    group "your-group-name"
        export "set-default-med"
    exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `entry 10` matches routes **without** a MED (`condition not med`) and sets their metric to 15000.  
- `entry 20` accepts all other routes unmodified.  
- The policy is applied as an `export` policy to the BGP group/neighbor to affect outbound route advertisements.  

Routes with existing metrics remain unchanged; only routes missing a metric are tagged with 15000.
