    exit
exit
```

Replace `<ip-address>` with the problematic neighbor's IP. This sets the keepalive interval to 10 seconds and the hold timer to 150 seconds (15 missed keepalives × 10 seconds). The session will reset if no messages are received within 150 seconds. 

**Note:**  
- The peer must negotiate a hold time of at least 150 seconds. If the peer proposes a lower hold time, the session will reset earlier. To enforce 150 seconds, add `min 150` to the `hold-time` command (use cautiously, as it may reject sessions with incompatible peers).  
- Always coordinate timer changes with the peer to ensure compatibility.
