To address the immediate drop of BGP sessions during physical link failures, configure the following commands on your Nokia 7750 SR. These settings disable peer tracking and adjust hold timers to allow brief session stalling, enabling redundant paths to activate before session teardown.

```cli
configure router bgp no enable-peer-tracking
configure router bgp hold-time 180 min 180
```

### Explanation:
- **`no enable-peer-tracking`**: Disables immediate BGP session termination when the route to a peer is lost. The session will wait for the hold timer to expire, providing time for alternate routes to converge.
- **`hold-time 180 min 180`**: Sets the hold time to 180 seconds (3 minutes) and enforces a minimum negotiated hold time of 180 seconds. This extends the failure window, allowing redundant paths to stabilize before the session resets.

### Apply to Specific Groups/Neighbors (Optional):
If global changes aren't suitable, apply the settings per group or neighbor:
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> no enable-peer-tracking
configure router bgp group <group-name> hold-time 180 min 180
```
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> no enable-peer-tracking
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> hold-time 180 min 180
```

Replace `<group-name>` and `<ip-address>` with your specific BGP group or neighbor details. Adjust the hold time values (e.g., `90`, `120`) based on your network convergence time.
