---
## Proposed answer:
To prevent routes from being reflected back to the originating neighbor in a BGP route reflector setup, enable the `split-horizon` feature. This ensures routes learned from a peer are not advertised back to the same peer. Apply the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    split-horizon
exit
```

This command can also be applied at the group or neighbor level if specific granularity is required. For example:

```cli
configure router bgp group "RR-CLIENTS"
    split-horizon
exit
